  "linkedin_input_block": "Project: Last-Mile Delivery Network | domain: Logistics - Last-Mile Delivery\nDataset: 1,000 rows, 365 days, 4 depots, provenance synthetic_portfolio\nFinding: 347 of 1,000 routes finish below break-even (34.7%), totalling 24,010 in losses against a net profit of 46,054\nFinding: 707 routes (70.7%) ran more than 0.5 overtime hours earned a 4.9% margin versus 15.9% for all other routes\nFinding: Driver labour shows the widest per-parcel gap: 0.48 higher on loss-making routes, across 43,033 parcels\nFinding: The riskiest 20% of routes by out-of-fold model score hold 72.1% of all losses, against 20% for random selection\nFinding: North Hub (cold climate) | Urban Dense is the weakest lane: 106 routes (10.6% of the total), -5.4% margin, 3,707 net loss\nTools and models: pandas: cleaning, feature engineering and aggregation; scikit-learn Logistic Regression: pre-dispatch loss-risk classifier with stratified cross-validation; KMeans and Isolation Forest: route segments and anomaly flags; Rule-based alert engine: action priority for every route; Scenario simulations: what-if cost and price lookups; Plotly and openpyxl: interactive dashboard and Excel report\nTarget audience: recruiters and hiring managers"
